@base = http://localhost:3000

### 1. add a truck
POST {{base}}/api/trucks
Content-Type: application/json

{"plate_number":"ABC-1234","device_id":"TRUCK-001"}

### 2. add a client
POST {{base}}/api/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{"company_name":"Sunrise Grocers"}

### 3. office dispatches the truck
POST {{base}}/api/dispatch
Content-Type: application/json

{"truck_id":1}

### 4. GPS pings BEFORE a trip exists (send this 3 times, change the numbers a little)
POST {{base}}/api/gps
Content-Type: application/json

{"device_id":"TRUCK-001","lat":14.3300,"lng":120.9400,"speed":30}

### 5. driver calls in the destination, trip is created
POST {{base}}/api/trips
Content-Type: application/json

{"truck_id":1,"client_id":1,"destination_lat":13.9400,"destination_lng":121.1600,"allowance_amount":3500}

### 6. GPS pings AFTER the trip exists (send several, move the lat/lng each time)
POST {{base}}/api/gps
Content-Type: application/json

{"device_id":"TRUCK-001","lat":14.2000,"lng":121.0000,"speed":55}

### 7. delivered
PATCH {{base}}/api/trips/1/delivered

### 8. truck is back, waybill submitted
PATCH {{base}}/api/trips/1/waybill
Content-Type: application/json

{"waybill_number":"WB-0001","stops":[{"client_id":1,"drop_type":"full","notes":"20 sacks"}]}

### 9. billing queue
GET {{base}}/api/trips/awaiting-billing

### 10. generate invoice
POST {{base}}/api/trips/1/invoice

### 11. mark paid
POST {{base}}/api/invoices/1/pay